pe {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490627} {:answer/id #uuid "55a1680b-477c-5c0b-94eb-9979f7a37072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2969aa96-f753-5b99-b7a8-4a6298263693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490588} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa62c7a-3eae-53d1-8bfb-2c44ea119440" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "622a3a58-55bb-5010-91b6-37bedd13a1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-253559" :question/problem "Consider the set $D=[\\sqrt{3},4).$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $sup(D).$\n\nThe supremum of a set $D$ is the {{field-1}} of $D.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $D$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $D$ is the smallest upper bound of $D.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $D$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge 4$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $D.$ Thus, the set $[4,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $D.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<4$ is **not** an upper bound of $D.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $D$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<4.$\n\nTherefore, $[4,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $D,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(D)=min[4,\\infty )=4.\n$$\n\nNotice that $4\\notin D.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe supremum of $D$ is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $D.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $D$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\ge 4\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $sup(D)=4\\notin D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cc0bbd3-ba25-5fd0-9b64-f33746e77c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487716} {:answer/id #uuid "712bb123-f03c-5bbb-9049-2ae6f776e6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487793} {:answer/id #uuid "72410791-1a6d-5c90-b6f7-7312d8ca4da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487796} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8029f6-c90e-5c0c-bfd4-81655fc8e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487836} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ab285f-819b-5164-92e2-6ee90a76aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d8029f6-c90e-5c0c-bfd4-81655fc8e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487836} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3798da6-3e26-54e4-8f7c-6af936e37df8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28cb24da-7ead-51cb-82fe-c700e5c2c25f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253865" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e39b8db15f47b0c07efec1b364f6fda7b3b7991ba13d71125505b1172937888.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n$\\,{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, $A$ has no lower bounds. We can always find an element $x$ such that $f(x)$ is smaller than $y$ for any $y.$ \n\nTherefore, ${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)$ $=-\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b8257c3-cb89-57e7-af23-191b90a42228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b8257c3-cb89-57e7-af23-191b90a42228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488647} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ad18e2-13e5-50fe-b40b-8175f7273995" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd9f0c45-62d6-5bab-b897-93c9f4793a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-253869" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5dc63d364beae0482fdb996372e5042e4c5edf2a6bdbd7a5b79dbcc55cf419cb.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,4].$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 4$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<4$ cannot be an upper bound of $A$ because $4,$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $[4,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[4,\\infty )=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e00bd87d-5f08-5393-9463-9cdcd001373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e00bd87d-5f08-5393-9463-9cdcd001373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c08a640-f274-5c79-a1a1-0eb159327882" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a350bae-823f-50ee-90ca-2add36d5d3d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253896" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d745d274250c84f6701ff22d17d0c6506a9f03f4a1a461e09f609a0ea11d99b.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=[-2,1).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 1$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<1$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $y$ for any $y<1.$\n\nTherefore, $[1,\\infty )$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[1,\\infty )=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560fbf54-d06b-5360-a195-76877c86b33e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486782} {:answer/id #uuid "5df91ad0-b4ef-5be9-8cb0-c61b9391c511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486804} {:answer/id #uuid "999b27c8-912c-51fc-a11a-66b74ddf77ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486941} {:answer/id #uuid "d577c117-bc3c-53e3-be7a-c468c23a624b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d577c117-bc3c-53e3-be7a-c468c23a624b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487061} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e3bb45-2a66-5b11-9cff-86ec4e98fa2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b171f8f-d26a-5943-99d9-8e4c4110d0e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-253899" :question/problem "![](images/56/567aa249f2ed84b537d20d4137a28e0df1cd3e4c942f4cf305bd864da32b8bac.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n$\\,{sup}_{x\\ge -1}f(x)$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=[0,\\infty ).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, $A$ has no upper bounds. We can always find an element $x$ such that $f(x)$ is greater than $y$ for any $y.$ \n\nTherefore, ${sup}_{x\\ge -1}f(x)$ $=+\\infty .$"}]}
